-- title:
--   Finite part at level Γ_H: membership criterion
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lying over $p$ in the sense that $p$ is a non-unit of $A$, whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data for the situation — in particular a morphism $\sigma_A \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{base}\,p$ lifting the generic point — and let $O$ be a `JHNeronObjectAtP` for $p, M, H, A$ and $\Lambda$, so that $O$ carries a scheme $G$ over $\mathrm{base}\,p$ with a relative group law and a bijection $O.\mathrm{pts}$ from $J_H(M) = \mathrm{Pic}^0$ of the base-changed function field `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ onto the sections of $G$ over the generic point. For $m \in \mathbb{N}$ and $x \in J_H(M)$, the assertion is that $x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, defined as the subgroup generated by those $y$ which are annihilated by $m$ in $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ and for which $O.\mathrm{pts}\,y$ factors as $\mathrm{barPt}\,A$ followed by some section of $G$ over $\sigma_A$, if and only if $x$ itself is annihilated by $m$ and $O.\mathrm{pts}\,x$ so factors. Thus membership in the generated subgroup unfolds to membership in the generating set.
--
--   This identifies the "finite part" subgroup attached to the Néron object of $J_H(M)$ at a prime $p$ dividing $M$: the $m$-torsion classes whose associated section over the generic point extends to a section over $\operatorname{Spec} A$. It is used whenever a concrete element of $\mathrm{finPts}$ must be handled directly, for instance in the divisibility of valuations of such classes, in the construction of configured representatives of classes in $\mathrm{finPts}$, and in the Atkin–Lehner analysis of the special fibre.
